# No Co-Authored Commits

Never add a `Co-authored-by:` trailer (or any co-author attribution) to git
commits. This includes `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: Claude`, or
any agent/tool attribution. Commits must contain only the message itself.

If the environment auto-appends a `Co-authored-by:` trailer when running
`git commit`, rebuild the commit without it using plumbing so the trailer never
lands:

```bash
tree=$(git rev-parse HEAD^{tree})
parent=$(git rev-parse HEAD^)
export GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=$(git log -1 --format='%an')
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=$(git log -1 --format='%ae')
export GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=$(git log -1 --format='%aI')
export GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=$(git log -1 --format='%cn')
export GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=$(git log -1 --format='%ce')
export GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=$(git log -1 --format='%cI')
new=$(git commit-tree "$tree" -p "$parent" -m "<commit message>")
git reset --hard "$new"
```

Always verify with `git log -1 --format='%B'` that no trailer remains.
